docs/findings.md:109:| E11 | 2026-09-17 | **Resolved 2026-09-18 (sandbox); the cause was ours and the docs page is wrong** | `m2-hip-link-care-context` refuses a request with **HTTP 400 and an empty body** (no content type, no code) when `hiType` is an **array**. It needs a **string**. The page types the field `object[]` and its own example sends `"hiType": ["Prescription"]`, so the page is wrong. Measured 2026-09-18 with 1 variable changed at a time, same token, same headers, same body: `hiType: ["DischargeSummary"]` answers the empty 400; `hiType: "DischargeSummary"` reaches the business logic and answers **202**, then `on_carecontext` answers `Successfully Linked care context`. A string that joins 2 types with a comma is refused in JSON: `Invalid HIType, it must be in Prescription,DiagnosticReport,OPConsultation,DischargeSummary,ImmunizationRecord,HealthDocumentRecord,WellnessRecord,Invoice`. To carry several HI types, send 1 `patient` block for each type in the same call, with the same `careContexts`; that answers 202 and the gateway sends 1 callback for the call (F7). The empty 400 is therefore a shape error the service does not name. **Order of the checks, measured 2026-09-17 12:34Z to 12:40Z.** A missing header answers an empty 401. A garbage `X-Link-Token` answers `ABDM-9999: Invalid X Auth token`. A body with `patient: []` answers `ABDM-9999: patient attribute required in the payload`. `X-HIP-ID` is not read before the shape check. Past the shape check, a bad field answers the empty 400 with no code. Every refusal comes from `server: istio-envoy` with `x-envoy-upstream-service-time` 16-25 ms and carries `correlation-id` and `activityid`; the plug keeps these in `AbdmOutboundRequest.response_headers`. **2 corrections to my earlier reading.** (1) I read the 500 `303001 ... HIECM-HIP-INITIATED-LINKING--vv3_APIproductionEndpoint [ State : SUSPENDED ]` as proof of an ABDM outage. It is not. The API manager suspends an endpoint after a transport failure and the state is transient; outbound rows 433 and 434 show the same code on a healthy API, `HIECM-LinkToken--vv3`, which answered 202 again 3 minutes later. (2) The check order above shows only that our token and our top-level shape pass, not that the whole body is right. The 1 field it does not cover, `hiType`, was the cause. **The page must name a code for this 400 and must type `hiType` as a string.** | `api/m2/endpoints/m2-hip-link-care-context`, `api/m2/errors` |
