docs/findings.md-120-| F1 | 2026-09-10 | **Open; the "immediately" reading is disproven 2026-09-17** | Link token lifetime conflict. `concepts/linking`, `milestones/m2`, the glossary and `how-it-fits` say "valid six months, stored at registration"; `m2-generate-link-token` says "short-lived ... must be called immediately before the linking call, tokens expire quickly". The JWT `exp` is `iat` + 182.5 days (F2). Token age is **not** the cause of E11: at 15:47:40.032 a token callback arrived and at 15:47:40.128, 96 ms later, the link call went out with a 2-second-old token and got the same empty HTTP 400. The plug's 5-minute freshness rule was therefore removed (ADR-012); it only forced a re-request inside the F6 window and earned `ABDM-1092`. The docs should say the token is valid 6 months, or state what "expire quickly" measures. | `concepts/linking`, `api/m2/endpoints/m2-generate-link-token` |
docs/findings.md-121-| F2 | 2026-09-15 | Resolved 2026-09-17 (sandbox) | The link token is a JWT, alg **RS512** (signed by the RS512 key in the gateway JWKS), claims `{hipId, abhaNumber (integer), transactionId, abhaAddress, sub (= abhaAddress), iat, exp}`; `exp - iat` = 15 768 000 s = 182.5 days, which is the "six months" of `concepts/linking`. The page should publish the claim set. | `concepts/linking`, `api/m2/endpoints/m2-on-generate-token-result` |
